WEBVTT

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.200
Kokomi, you have practice this morning, right?

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:33.840
Wake up.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.610
Good morning.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.360
Good morning.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.200
Good morning, Kokomi.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.560
You'd better eat quickly or you'll be late.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:00.730
Thanks for breakfast.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.280
You have practice this morning?

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.750
Is there a tournament coming up?

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.040
She's hoping to place in 
the prefectural tournament.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.130
You'll have to work hard.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.300
Right!

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.260
I'm going now!

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:15.850
Take care!

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:04.970
<b>Our First Promise</b>

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.910
Good morning!

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.080
Good morning.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.040
Morning!

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:15.540
I'm going to need to add more fertilizer soon.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.260
That's right.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:19.800
Tachibana-sensei!

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.910
Good morning!

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.180
Good morning, Kamijou-san,

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.420
Shigetou-san.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:29.140
Good morning, Tachibana-sensei!

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:31.020
Good morning, Shiina-san.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.270
Oh, good morning.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.130
Keep at it, Kumada-san.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.040
Harumiya-san!

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.700
Good morning!

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.910
Good morning, Shiina-san!

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:50.600
Good luck at practice!

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.410
Right!

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.670
Ah, Shiina-senpai.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:57.730
It's almost time for your rhythmic 
gymnastics tournament, right?

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.810
It's the Sunday after next.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:03.040
There's not much time left, 
so I'm a little worried.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.460
You'll be fine, Shiina-senpai!

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:06.550
I'm rooting for you!

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.280
Thank you, Hazuki-san.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:21.690
All right.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.120
Good morning, Shiina-san.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.450
Good morning.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.440
That was close.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.900
Mochizuki-senpai.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.070
Sorry about that...

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.110
Did I distract you?

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:09.780
Sorry, I'm not good with having my 
picture taken while I'm practicing.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:14.540
But you were just so cute, Kokomi-chan.

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:16.200
Senpai...

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.390
Could you pose like that again for me?

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:20.790
Huh?

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.400
Those things are "clubs," right?

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.940
It looked really pretty when 
you were tossing them around.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.550
Could you do it one more time?

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.810
Um... Mochizuki-senpai...

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.890
You're so adorable, Kokomi-chan.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.050
Um...

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:42.820
I can't focus when people are watching me...

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:43.880
I'm sorry.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:44.920
Really?

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:48.070
It'll be even better practice 
for your competitions, then.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:48.940
Huh?

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.480
I'll watch you.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.240
That way, you can practice your concentration.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.020
No, that's not what I...

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:00.800
Non, non. Erena-san, that's no good.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.720
Who's there?

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.710
I'm Chloe Lemaire.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:09.340
Practice is a sacred thing.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:13.230
No one should interfere.

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:17.430
I think your request is extremely selfish.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.350
I can't?

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:21.150
No.

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:23.720
That's too bad.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.350
Fine.

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:26.740
Hm?

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.900
Next time, let me get some pictures of you

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.490
when you're done with practice.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:32.040
Huh?

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.840
See you later, Kokomi-chan.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:40.140
Erena-san is just impossible.

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.860
I'm sorry.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.850
She just really likes girls.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:48.600
I don't think she means any harm.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.250
No, not at all.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.520
Thank you, Lemaire-san.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.970
I know of you.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:55.890
Huh?

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.530
Kokomi Shiina-san.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:58.720
A second-year.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:00.780
A cute and pretty girl.

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:02.950
Th-Thank you.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:03.880
Oh, yeah.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:06.520
Do you know what this means?

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:09.990
"Mimi in the wall, Mary in the door."

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:10.990
Mary?

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.450
Are they sisters? Friends?

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.860
And why is Mimi in a wall?

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:24.130
Um, the "Mimi" isn't a girl's name. 
It's the Japanese word for "ears."

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:25.160
Oh!

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:27.750
And "Mary" is "me ari," which means "have eyes."

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:28.760
Oh, my!

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:33.250
So it's "The walls have ears 
and the doors have eyes."

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:35.710
It's a Japanese idiom that means you never know

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:40.000
who's listening to you or watching you, 
even if you're being secretive,

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.160
so you should be careful what you say and do.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:45.280
Oh, très bien!

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:47.120
Wonderful.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.650
What a wonderfully literary expression.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:55.510
Now I can add something 
new to my Japan notebook.

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.640
Thank you!

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:00.940
Um, you're welcome.

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:05.080
Will you teach me more things, Kokomi-san?

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.840
Sure, if I can.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.480
Merci, Kokomi-san.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:12.000
Let us meet again.

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:22.320
This is...

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.170
Hm? Kokomi-chan?

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.320
What's wrong?

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:41.410
Um, have you seen Lemaire-san?

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:43.530
Lemaire-san?

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:45.430
The third-year girl?

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:49.130
I just got here, so I'm not sure.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:52.010
Hm?

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:54.340
You better get changed, or you'll be late.

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:56.680
Oh, yeah!

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.710
I made it in time...

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:09.460
Sorry!

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:13.180
Good morning, Sagara-san.

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:15.210
Practicing your juggling?

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:16.620
Thanks.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.520
I can do four balls at once, but...

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:23.950
It's always hard to handle props in gymnastics.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.840
Yeah, clubs are really hard, too, right?

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:29.970
How do you do it, Kokomi-chan?

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:33.840
I think the trick is to make use 
of their centrifugal force.

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:35.560
Centrifugal force?

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:37.970
It's a snap of the wrist.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.040
I get it.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:40.340
A snap, huh?

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:43.320
But if you try to catch their 
weight with just your wrists,

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.360
it's easy to hurt yourself, so be careful.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:46.700
Got it!

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:49.310
How is that finger you jammed the other day?

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:51.880
Saeki-san took a look at it for me.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.820
It's fine now.

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.040
Looks good to me.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:09:59.400
It doesn't feel feverish, either.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:00.490
That's good.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.700
Marika-chan, you're like the 
nightingale of Seiou Academy.

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:05.910
I'm on the health committee.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.490
I have to know this stuff.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:09.650
Um, I have a question.

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:10.170
Hm?

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:13.880
Do you know Chloe Lemaire-san, the third-year?

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:14.940
Of course.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:17.360
She's famous throughout the school.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:21.120
I only know she's a French exchange student.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.060
Yeah, so she's living in the dorms.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.730
Apparently, she's really interested in Japan.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:28.580
The other day, she came to the nurse's office

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:31.100
and took pictures of the eye chart.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.980
She said it was different from French ones.

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:35.430
She's even interested in stuff like that?

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:36.200
Yeah.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:38.200
Do you know what class she's in?

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.990
Class A, I believe.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.440
Why?

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.550
There's something I'd like to return to her.

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:46.240
Good morning, everyone.

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:48.580
Good morning.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.760
It's almost the season for fall tournaments,

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:57.260
the cultural fair, and other events,

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.880
but I want you all to make sure you're careful

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:01.560
not to injure yourselves.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.910
S-Sorry!

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.150
I was spacing out...

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:24.660
Oh, I'm sorry, too.

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:26.660
The student council president!

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.960
My name's Kanata Amatsu.

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:33.290
And you're... Kokomi Shiina-san, correct?

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.560
You know who I am?

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:35.920
Yes.

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.610
You're famous.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.200
You're the ace of the rhythmic gymnastics team.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.090
I've seen many of your performances,

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.530
and they were all wonderful!

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.230
Thank you very much.

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:50.880
President, where are you going?

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:53.730
You still have all this work left to do.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:56.320
Oh, my. What a problem.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:12:00.270
You promised to read over this 
material by the end of today.

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:04.240
Can't I just leave that to you, Mutsumi-chan?

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.230
No, you can't.

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.930
I'm just the secretary.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:09.180
But...

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:12.920
I won't spoil you like the vice president does.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:16.060
You're so strict, Mutsumi-chan.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:18.560
By the way, Shiina-san.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:23.630
You're a second-year, so why were 
you in a third-year classroom?

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:27.490
I'm actually looking for Lemaire-san.

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:28.430
Let's see.

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:31.810
She was here until just a second ago...

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:35.820
Chloe-san tends to appear and 
disappear unexpectedly.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:37.180
Do you need her for something?

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:38.220
Yes.

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:42.940
If you have any idea where she might be, 
I'd appreciate it if you could tell me.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:44.910
Well...

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:48.430
I see her in the library quite often.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:51.500
How about taking a look in the library?

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.110
It seems like she's always researching something.

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:55.420
I will.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.810
Thank you very much.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:10.880
Stand.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:11.600
Bow.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.120
Oh, excuse me!

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:24.070
You seem to be in quite the hurry.

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:25.390
I'm sorry.

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:26.980
Good timing.

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:29.070
I wanted to interview you 
for the school newspaper.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:30.780
Interview?

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:31.500
Yes.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.200
I'm gathering comments from prominent athletes

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.850
who are participating in the fall tournaments.

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:37.830
Comments?

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:38.880
Well...

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:41.210
Let's start with what you hope to achieve.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:45.040
Well, I am trying to place 
higher than I did last year.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.980
Are you trying to make it to nationals?

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:49.630
Yes, I'd like to go, if possible.

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:54.900
For that, I need to get a good rank 
in the prefectural tournament first.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:57.480
Oh, Kokomi-chan and Saya-san.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.440
What are you two doing here?

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.810
I'm interviewing Shiina-san.

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:04.450
How wonderful.

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:06.900
When will that be printed?

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.810
We're shooting for next week.

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:11.090
Hm? What's wrong, Shiina-san?

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:11.730
Huh?

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:12.830
Your face is red.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.870
No, it's nothing.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:17.460
Oh, dear. Do you have a fever?

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.000
Sasahara-senpai...

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.030
This is terrible.

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:22.840
You're burning up.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:24.410
Are you okay?

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:25.670
Do you need to go to the nurse's office?

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.790
No, I'm fine.

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:29.790
But you're really feverish...

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:32.110
It's nothing, really!

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:37.920
Excuse me, Sasahara-senpai, 
Kagurazaka-senpai.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:54.310
Girl Friend BETA.

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:13.350
Good afternoon!

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:17.390
How is everyone spending their lunch break?

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:21.310
<i>This is Akane Sakurai, 
and I'll be your host every week,</i>

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:24.100
<i>Mondays, Tuesdays, and Thursdays, 
with upbeat music and fun talks</i>

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:27.820
<i>to liven up your lunch breaks at Seiou Academy.</i>

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:31.700
<i>Okay, it's now time for "Q & Akane,"</i>

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:38.450
<i>where I'll answer any questions 
or worries you might have!</i>

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:46.210
Um...

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:51.160
You're Fumio Murakami-san, on the 
librarian committee, correct?

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:51.590
Yes.

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:54.710
I'm Kokomi Shiina, a second-year.

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:58.720
Is Chloe Lemaire-san here?

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:01.300
I haven't seen her today.

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:05.980
She was here yesterday, saying she 
wanted to research flower arrangement.

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:07.230
Flower arrangement?

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:08.850
Yes.

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:10.240
Do you need her for something?

00:16:10.710 --> 00:16:13.510
Yes. I have something to give to her.

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:16.400
Do you think she might be in the 
flower arrangement club room?

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:17.840
It's possible.

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:22.170
She's been rather interested in flower 
arrangement and tea ceremonies lately.

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:24.200
She might be there.

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:26.580
Thank you.

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:27.720
I'll check it out.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:35.050
<b>Flower Arrangement Club</b>

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:43.290
Well, lunch break is almost over.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:47.480
So, everyone, good luck 
in your afternoon classes!

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.860
See you. Bye-bye!

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.620
Good work.

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.130
You, too.

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:59.400
I stuttered a little bit.

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:01.890
Really? I couldn't tell at all.

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:03.870
It was fine!

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:09.090
It was because the negotiations broke down that...

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:25.560
See you later.

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:29.320
Let's stop by the café.

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:30.510
I'm so hungry.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:32.950
I'm in! I really want some lemonade.

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:35.130
He still isn't back.

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:36.990
Yeah. I wonder where he is.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:38.950
How far did he go, anyway?

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:42.120
<i>I'm sure this picture is important to her.</i>

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:44.040
<i>I'd like to give it back to her today.</i>

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:47.200
<b>Flower Arrangement Club</b>

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:56.490
Haruko, the flowers that you bring us

00:17:56.490 --> 00:17:59.590
are always so lively.

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:06.030
That's because you arrange them
 so thoughtfully, Isuzu-chan.

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:06.800
Hm?

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:07.640
Excuse me.

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:12.670
I'm sorry, but is Lemaire-san here?

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:15.320
She left not too long ago.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.780
Huh? Where was she going?

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.160
Who knows?

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:21.260
The library, the courtyard, the athletic field...

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:23.240
Or maybe the science classroom?

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:26.040
She never stays in one place long.

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:28.510
Who knows where she went?

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:32.990
She's always flitting about, like a butterfly.

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:34.510
I see...

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:47.470
<i>The library, the gymnasium, 
the science classroom...</i>

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.760
<i>She wasn't in any of them...</i>

00:18:57.000 --> 00:19:01.410
Now that I think about it, I didn't eat lunch today.

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:14.000
That's Kokomi-san.

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:20.730
<i>If I don't see her today,</i>

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:24.360
<i>maybe I should wait outside 
her class early tomorrow.</i>

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:25.600
Octopus hot dogs!

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.820
L-Lemaire-san?!

00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:33.160
Japanese lunches are so beautiful.

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:35.610
Could I take a picture?

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:37.030
G-Go ahead.

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:42.840
Meatballs, baby tomatoes, onigiri...

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:44.530
They're all wonderful.

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:48.650
I love the fried egg, especially.

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:50.790
W-Would you like some?

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:53.430
Oui! Oui!

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:02.180
It's not sweet!

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:03.480
Huh?

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:06.750
The fried egg sushi I had was sweet,

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:10.200
but your fried egg isn't.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:11.360
I'm sorry.

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:13.060
You didn't like it?

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:15.440
Non! That's not it!

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.050
It's delicious.

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:19.120
I loved it!

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:20.240
C'est bon!

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:21.810
I'm glad.

00:20:24.440 --> 00:20:28.310
I heard you were looking for me.

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:32.200
Kanata-san, Saya-san, Fumio-san, Isuzu-san...

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:34.200
Lots of people told me.

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:37.080
The walls have ears and the doors have eyes.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:40.800
And Seiou Academy has Chloe Lemaire!

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:45.130
Oh, yeah. Actually...

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:48.760
This is your photo, right?

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:50.250
Oh, my.

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:53.050
Where did you find it?

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:54.850
In the gymnasium this morning.

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:58.550
Did I drop it?

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:01.170
I didn't even notice.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:05.410
So, this is why you were searching for me?

00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:06.980
Yes.

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:09.160
I wanted to give it back 
to you as soon as I could.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:15.040
L-Lemaire-san?!

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.300
Merci, Kokomi-san!

00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:20.400
That picture means a lot to me!

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:24.270
I'm sure I would have been 
very sad if I had lost it.

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:28.050
I didn't think you'd be so happy, Lemaire-san...

00:21:28.570 --> 00:21:31.870
Non! Call me Chloe.

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:32.600
Huh?

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.200
Lemaire is my last name.

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:35.920
Chloe is my name.

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:38.310
And I'll call you Kokomi.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:40.690
Oh...

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:42.120
Okay,

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:44.320
Chloe-san.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:45.760
Oui!

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:48.310
I'd like to thank you.

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:50.480
What would you like?

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:53.720
I'll do whatever you want, Kokomi.

00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:55.200
You don't need to thank me.

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:57.150
Non, non!

00:21:57.150 --> 00:22:00.280
I'm going to do something for you!

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:01.470
Um...

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:03.720
Um...

00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:07.720
Can I not do anything for you?

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:10.860
Huh? Um, well...

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:15.650
Can you let me think about it for a little while?

00:22:15.650 --> 00:22:18.370
When I decide on something, I'll ask you.

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:19.740
Of course!

00:22:19.740 --> 00:22:22.420
Promise on <i>harakiri!</i>

00:22:22.890 --> 00:22:24.720
That's not right, Chloe-san!

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:27.160
It's <i>yubikiri</i> (pinky swear), not <i>harakiri.</i>

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:29.530
Tee-hee. I messed up.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:24.600
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:11.240 --> 00:24:12.750
Kokomi Shiina here.

00:24:12.750 --> 00:24:14.320
I feel like I've never done

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:16.180
a perfect performance since

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:18.310
I started rhythmic gymnastics.

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:20.680
I need to try harder.

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:22.860
Next time: Blue Melon Buns.

00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:24.600
<b>Episode 2: Blue Melon Buns</b>

00:24:22.860 --> 00:24:24.600
I hope you'll watch.
